{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ea867254344d6c8f4c523beb97738fcb1ac636ce103b46f8f9cc243ccdaef1c7","digest":{"component_or_area":"documentation (writing-a-passing-plan guide)","key_entities":["docs/writing-a-passing-plan.md","rebar citation","[rebar:<id>]","det_citation._edge_verified","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_citation.py","depends_on","blocks"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","citation requirement","direct edge","transitive dependency","verification"],"propositions":["The `[rebar:<id>]` citation section in docs/writing-a-passing-plan.md does not explicitly state that the upstream edge must be DIRECT.","The verifier `det_citation._edge_verified` correctly checks only direct edges (no recursion), so transitive/indirect dependencies do not satisfy the citation requirement.","Users can create citations with transitive dependencies that fail verification with no warning, because the documentation does not clarify the direct-edge requirement.","The fix is documentation-only: add clarification that the edge must be DIRECT and that transitive/indirect dependencies do not count.","The verifier implementation already matches the intended behavior, so no code changes are needed."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787738666771913001,"uuid":"68b4a7da-b470-4304-8a19-a92d1b786801"}